025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Lombardo\uc1 \u8217 ?s translation feels immediately like a breath of fresh air: the verse is energetic, colloquial, crisp, and enticing; the diction is immediately accessible to the inexperienced reader, and the flexible rhythm keeps the poem moving. Lombardo is willing to depart from a strict literal fidelity to the original Greek in order to bring the poem closer to the modern imagination and makes no attempt to inject a strained loftiness or olde worlde vocabulary into his descriptions or dialogue. One of his striking innovations\uc1 \u8212 ?placing the Homeric similes in italics in their own paragraphs\uc1 \u8212 ?is also an extremely effective way of emphasizing the importance and impact of these (often overlooked) elements of Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s style.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 These qualities obviously come with a price. Readers may well find the style too direct and breezy, too far removed from the more solemn and lofty gravitas they expect in an ancient poem. They may feel that the tug of war between past and present (inevitably a part of the translation of an ancient epic) has here been resolved too easily in favour of our modern times, especially in the dialogue, which makes frequent use of modern slang: \uc1 \u8220 ?goddamn,\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?pansy,\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?badmouth,\uc1 \u8221 ? and \uc1 \u8220 ?man\uc1 \u8221 ? as a term of address (as in the modern expression \uc1 \u8220 ?Hey, man, . . .\uc1 \u8221 ?).}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Whether Lombardo\uc1 \u8217 ?s bold diction amounts to what one reviewer has called a \uc1 \u8220 ?dumbing down\uc1 \u8221 ? of Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s epic or adds to the vitality and impact of the style is obviously up to the reader. In general, I like what Lombardo has done, but there are certainly moments when (reluctantly) I have to stop because some distinctively modern colloquial word or phrase has interrupted my imaginative contact with Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s world.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 For a longer preview of Lombardo\uc1 \u8217 ?s }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Iliad}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 , please use the following link: }{\field \fldedit {\*\fldinst {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.ca/Iliad-Homer/dp/0872203522/ref=sr_1_1?ie=UTF8&qid=1511895508&sr=8-1&keywords=lombardo+iliad&asin=0872203522&revisionId=&format=4&depth=1" }}{\fld