e next }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 and}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  (hard not to do, given the frequency of the word) this stylistic feature can get quite irritating.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Mitchell, like some other translators, also has trouble establishing a consistently satisfying diction. For the most part, his language is sufficiently clear and direct, but there are times when the insertion of a modern colloquial expression (\uc1 \u8220 ?son of a bitch,\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?sissy,\uc1 \u8221 ? \uc1 \u8220 ?open his trap,\uc1 \u8221 ? and so on) seems rather at odds with his desire to get back to the purity of the original. People\uc1 \u8217 ?s reactions to such sudden reminders of a distinctively modern slangy idiom vary, of course, so what one reader may accept as a vivid and appropriate contemporary expression another may well deplore as an unwelcome interruption of her imaginative contact with Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s world (not an uncommon complaint with Lombardo\uc1 \u8217 ?s translation, as well).}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 All that said, this translation is well worth the reader\uc1 \u8217 ?s attention, and someone seeking a text of the }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 Iliad}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025  for classroom use should certainly consider it. I suspect, however, that many teachers in search of a full text of a translated }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp