s0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \qc \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 What Went On in the House of Odysseus}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 THIS IS THE STORY OF A MAN, ONE WHO WAS NEVER AT A loss. He had travelled far in the world, after the sack of Troy, the virgin fortress; he saw many cities of men, and learnt their mind; he endured many troubles and hardships in the struggle to save his own life and to bring back his men safe to their homes. He did his best, but he could not save his companions. For they perished by their own madness, because they killed and ate the cattle of Hyperion the Sun-god, and the }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 god took care that they should never see home again.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025    At the time when I begin, all the others who had not been killed in the war were at home, safe from the perils of battle and sea: but he was alone, longing to get home to his wife. He was kept prisoner by a witch, Calypso, a radiant creature, and herself one of the great family of gods, who wanted him to stay in her cave and be her husband. Well, then, the seasons went rolling by, and when the year came, in which by the thread that fate spins for every man he was to return home to Ithaca, he had not yet got free of his troubles and come back to his own people. The gods were all sorry for him, except Poseidon, god of the sea, who bore a lasting grudge against him all the time until he returned.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025    But it happened that Poseidon went for a visit a long way off, to the Ethiopians; who live at the ends of the earth, some near the sunrise, some near the sunset. There he expected a fine sacrifice of bulls and goats, and there he was, feasting an enjoying himself mightily; but the other gods were all gathered in the palace of Olympian Zeus.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025    Then the Father of gods and men made them a speech; for his heart was angry against a man, Aigisthos, and Agamemnon\uc1 \u8217 ?s son Orestes, as you know, had just killed the man. So he spoke to the company as follows:}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025    \uc1 \u8220 ?Upon my word, just see how mortal men always put the blame on us gods! We are the source of evil, so they say\uc1 \u8212 ?when they have only their own madness to thank if their miseries are worse than they ought to be. Look here, now: Aigisthos has done what he ought not to have done. Took Agamemnon\uc1 \u8217 ?s wedded wife for himself, killed Agamemnon when he came home, though he knew quite well it would be his own ruin! We gave him fair warning, sent our special messenger Hermes, and told him not to kill the man or to make love to his wife; their son Orestes would punish him, when he grew up and wanted his own dominions. Hermes told him plainly, but he could do nothing with Aigisthos, although it was for his good. Now he has paid the debt in one lump sum.\uc1 \u8221 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 REVIEW COMMENT}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Rouse\uc1 \u8217 ?s original translation bears the sub-title \uc1 \u8220 ?The Adventures of Ulysses\uc1 \u8221 ? and he must be among the last translators to use the old Latin names (although that has changed in more recent editions of his translation).\uc1 \u160 ?\uc1 \u160 ?Strictly speaking, this title should not be included on a list of complete English translations of the\uc1 \u160 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Odyssey}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 , because Rouse, in his desire to deliver a rendition of Homer in modern colloquial prose for everyman, takes considerable liberties with Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s text.\uc1 \u160 ?However, in its day the translation was well known, and it is still in print (as a Signet Classic) and available online.\uc1 \u160 ?Anyone seeking a prose translation of Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s\uc1 \u160 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Odyssey}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \uc1 \u160 ?should, in the interest of getting Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s poem relatively unsullied, select another version, but Rouse is worth browsing for his no}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 -}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 nonsense brusque energetic prose (larded with the occasional odd piece of antique diction). }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs28 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs28 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 \page }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs28 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs28 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\*\bkmkstart odysseyrieu}{\*\bkmkend odysseyrieu}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Homer}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 The Odyssey}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Translated by E. V. Rieu}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 London 1946}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 (Revised 1991)}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Sample from the Opening of the Revised Edition}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 I}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 ATHENE VISITS}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 TELEMACHUS}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1  Tell me, Muse, the story of that resourceful man who was driven to wander far and wide after he had sacked the holy citadel of Troy. He saw the cities of many people and he learnt their ways. He suffered great anguish on the high seas in his struggles to preserve his life and bring his comrades home. But he failed to save those comrades, in spite of all his efforts. It was their own transgression that brought them to their doom, for in their folly they devoured the oxen of Hyperion the Sun-god and he saw to it that they would never return. Tell us this story, goddess daughter of Zeus, beginning at whatever point you will.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 All the survivors of the war had reached their homes by now and so put the perils of battle and the sea behind them. Odysseys alone was prevented from returning to the home and wife he yearned for by that powerful goddess, the Nymph Calypso, who longed for him to marry her, and kept him in her vaulted cave. Not even when the rolling seasons brought in the year which the gods had chosen for his homecoming to Ithaca was he clear of his troubles and safe among his friends. Yet all the gods pitied him, except Poseidon, who pursued the heroic Odyssey with relentless malice till the day when he reached his own country.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Poseidon, however, was now gone on a visit to the distant Ethiopians, in the most remote part of the world, half of whom live where the Sun goes down, and half where he rises. He had gone to accept a sacrifice of bulls and rams, and there he sat and enjoyed the pleasures of the feast. Meanwhile the rest of the gods had assembled in the palace of Olympian Zeus, and the Father of men and gods opened a discussion among them. He had been thinking of the handsome Aegisthus, whom Agamemnon\uc1 \u8217 ?s far-famed son Orestes killed; and it was with Aegisthus in his mind that Zeus now addressed the immortals:}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \uc1 \u8216 ?What a lamentable thing it is that men should blame the gods and regard us as the source of their troubles, when it is their own transgressions which bring them suffering that was not their destiny. Consider Aegisthus: it was not his destiny to steal Agamemnon\uc1 \u8217 ?s wife and murder her husband when he came home. He knew the result would be utter disaster, since we ourselves had sent Hermes, the keen-eyed Giant-slayer, to warn him neither to kill the man nor to court his wife. For Orestes, as Hermes told him, was bound to avenge Agamemnon as soon as he grew up and thought with longing of his home. Yet with all his friendly counsel Hermes failed to dissuade him. And now Aegisthus has paid the final price for all his sins.\uc1 \u8217 ?}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1  }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 REVIEW COMMENT}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1  Rieu\uc1 \u8217 ?s translation is a personal favourite of mine, since it was my introduction to Homer. In its day it was extremely popular, and it is still top of the list for the reader who is looking for a prose translation of Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Odyssey}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 , especially since the edition has been revised by Peter Jones and D. C. H. Rieu.  There\uc1 \u8217 ?s an interesting and brief introduction explaining some of the revisions they have made.  The translation is accurate, idiomatic, and dramatic, far superior to Martin Hammond\uc1 \u8217 ?s prose version.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 Rieu does have his critics (of course), some of whom object that he tones down the poem to something less majestic than it should be (\uc1 \u8220 ?[Rieu] converts Homer into treacle\uc1 \u8221 ? is the way John Crossett\uc1 \u8212 ?somewhat hyperbolically\uc1 \u8212 ?puts it) or that he turns the poem into a Victorian novel (as Adam Parry observed \uc1 \u8220 ?Rieu had discovered that Homer was really Trollope\uc1 \u8221 ?). But if this is treacle, there\uc1 \u8217 ?s nothing about it which slows the reader down or gives him an overdose of saccharine sweetness.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb0 \sa120 \sbauto0 \saauto0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 The reader who would like a preview of the revised Rieu translation should use the following link: }{\field \fldedit {\*\fldinst {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1  HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.ca/Odyssey-Homer/dp/0140449116?asin=0140449116&revisionId=&format=4&depth=1" }}{\fldrslt {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs15 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf14 \ul Rieu }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs15 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \cf14 \ul Odyssey}}}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs15 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \cf14 \ul }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs28 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs28 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 .}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs28 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs28 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs28 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs28 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 \page }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs28 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs28 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af6 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\*\bkmkstart odysseyrees}{\*\bkmkend odysseyrees}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 The Odyssey of Homer}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 Translated by}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 Ennis Rees}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 New York, 1960}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 I have been unable to find a copy of Ennis Rees's translation of the }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 Odyssey}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 . I did, however, stumble across a short review of the work, a portion of which I offer below, not because I think it is a fair evaluation of Rees's translation, but because I think it is a splendid example of a certain attitude one occasionally comes across in the Classics professoriate:}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 Of the present translation, it may suffice to quote the publishers' own description: 'Brilliantly done, in natural, free flowing verse, it is the most readable version available to modern readers.' If that does not deter buyers on this side of the Atlantic, the translator's own claims (p. xv) may be more effective; he writes: 'I have tried to be faithful to the sentiments, ideas and images of the original and to include whatever is necessary to the literal sense of the Greek poem. But I have also done what I could to make a readable English poem.' Such claims, as we know, are beyond the measure of human capacity to satisfy; and when it is }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 realised}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 , as it will soon be by those who pass beyond the preface to the translation itself, that Mr. Rees has no adequate knowledge either of Homeric Greek or what we still possessively regard as English, we shall, without a pang of regret, leave the book to be praised by those for whom it seems to have been intended.\uc1 \u160 ? (J. A. Davison, }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \cs16 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 The Classical Review}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 , Vol 12 Issue 3, December 1962, p. 303)}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 Another academic reviewer of the Rees translation raises an issue which has become increasingly evident in the translations of Homer in the past decades: the habit of offering Homer in what has come to be known as \uc1 \u8220 ?stacked prose\uc1 \u8221 ?:}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 This new translation of the }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 Odyssey}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1  is printed as though it were verse. The translator, moreover, tells us in the introduction, \uc1 \u8220 ?In meter the line I have found best suit for rendering the original dactylic hexameters is a loose measure of five major stresses plus a varying number of relatively unaccented syllables.\uc1 \u8221 ? Unable myself to feel that I was reading verse, but conscious of my limitations, I typed off as prose the following passage from the second paragraph of Rees\uc1 \u8217 ?s version (a fair sample, as far as I can tell): \uc1 \u8220 ?Now all the others who had managed to escape destruction were safe at home, untroubled by war or the sea. Odysseus alone, full of longing for wife and friends, was kept from returning by that beautiful nymph Calypso, the powerful goddess who hoped to make him her husband. Even in the year of his predestined return, at home among his own people, his toils were many.\uc1 \u8221 ? To this I added translations of the same passage by Rieu, Rouse, and Shaw. These anonymous extracts were then presented to a number of colleagues, who were asked to say which, if any, they felt might have been intended as verse. (I was careful not to choose classicists, and for the most part chose younger members of the English Department.) All were agreed that all the translations were prose. When I told them that one was said by the author to be verse and pressed them to pick which one this might be, their choices were varied, but no one chose Rees. Can it be that, like a famous predecessor, Rees has been using prose without realizing it? }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \line }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1    Though obviously not all his readers will be conscious of any metrical pattern in his rendering, Rees himself apparently is. At least I assume that it must be this subtle sense which causes him to pad his lines at times with words which have no counterpart in the original and are not necessary for the English sense. (Frederick Combellack, }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 Classical Philology}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 , Volume 57, Number 1, p. 60)}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 The phrase \uc1 \u8220 ?stacked prose\uc1 \u8221 ? is a commonly used pejorative to describe this modern tendency:}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 The original lines of Homer are ignored and the text is translated in prose. What makes stacked prose different from prose is that after the text starts at the left margin it only goes on for a set number of syllables before breaking to start the next line. This is done so that the text may look and read like verse, but while stacked prose mimics verse, a line of verse shows a strict poetic structure and forms a unit of composition, a line in stacked prose does not.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  (https://iliad-translations.com/ translation-comparison/).}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 This habit blurs the distinction between poetry and prose (presumably under the banner of \uc1 \u8220 ?free verse\uc1 \u8221 ?) since increasing the only major difference between the two is that printed prose has a more or less even right justification, whereas poetry has an erratic blank space to the right of the printed text.}{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf8 \page }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af4 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\*\bkmkstart odysseyfitzgerald}{\*\bkmkend odysseyfitzgerald}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Homer}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 The Odyssey}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Translated by Robert Fitzgerald}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 (New York 1961)}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Sample from the Opening of the Poem}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 [This sample does not reproduce the accents on some of the names.]}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Sing in me, Muse, and through me tell the story}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 of that man skilled in all ways of contenting,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the wanderer, harried for years on end,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 after he plundered the stronghold}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 on the proud height of Troy.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8                                               He saw the townlands}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 and learned the minds of many distant men,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 and weathered many bitter nights and days}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 in his deep heart at sea, while he fought only}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 to save his life, to bring his shipmates home.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 But not by will nor valor could he save them,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 for their own recklessness destroyed them all--}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 children and fools, they killed and feasted on}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the cattle of Lord Helios, the Sun,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 and he who moves all day through heaven}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 took from their eyes the dawn of their return.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Of these adventures, Muse, daughter of Zeus,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 tell us in our time, lift the great song again.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Begin when all the rest who left behind them}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 headlong death in battle or at sea}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 had long ago returned, while he alone still hungered}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 for home and wife. Her ladyship Kalypso}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 cling to him in her sea hollowed caves--}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 a nymph, immortal and most beautiful,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 who craved him for her own.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8                                               And when long years and seasons}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 wheeling brought around that point of time}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 ordained for him to make his passage homeward,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 trials and dangers, even so, attended him}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 even in Ithaca, near those he loved.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Yet all the gods had pitied Lord Odysseus,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 all but Poseidon, raging cold and rough}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 against the brave king till he came ashore}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 at last on his own land.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8                                      But now that god}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 had gone far off among the sunburnt races,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 most remote of men, at earth's two verges,I}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 n sunset lands and lands of the rising sun,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 to be regaled by smoke of thighbones burning,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 haunches of rams and bulls, a hundred fold.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 He lingered delighted at the banquet side.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 In the bright hall of Zeus upon Olympus}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the other gods were all at home, and Zeus,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the father of gods and men, made conversation.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 For he had meditated on Aigisthos, dead}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 by the hand of Agamemnon's son, Orestes,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 and spoke his thought aloud before them all.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \uc1 \u8220 ?My word, how mortals take the gods the task!}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 All their afflictions come from us, we hear.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 And what of their own failings? Greed and folly}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 double the suffering in the lot of man.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 See how Aigisthos, for his double portion,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 stole Agamemnon's wife and killed the soldier}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 on his homecoming day. And yet Aigisthos}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 knew that his own doom lay in this. We gods}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 had warned him, sent down Hermes Argeiphontes,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 our most observant courier, to say;}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 'Don't kill the man, don't touch his wife,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 or face a reckoning with Orestes}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the day he comes of age and wants his patrimony.'}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Friendly advice--but would Aigisthos take it?}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Now he has paid the reckoning in full.\uc1 \u8221 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 REVIEW COMMENT}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Fitzgerald\uc1 \u8217 ?s }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Odyssey}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  is one of the best, if not the best, modern rendition of Homer into English verse, mainly because Fitzgerald is a much more accomplished poet than his competitors and because he understands better than almost all his fellow translators (ancient and modern) how best to reconcile the demands of the Greek text with the requirements of a modern readership. He also knows how to use the iambic pentameter line to convey the energy, speed, and beauty of Homer\uc1 \u8217 ?s original, without being sidetracked by misleading notions of fidelity to the Greek metre or to the original sound of the poem (notions which have infected a number of modern translations): he has \uc1 \u8220 ?paid less attention to the technicalities of his Homeric verse and more to an inventive American style in [his] mother tongue\uc1 \u8221 ? (McCrorie).}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 This translation places Fitzgerald in the tradition of the best and most successful translators of Homer who have rendered the Greek in extraordinarily expressive poetry of their own age:}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Fitzgerald\uc1 \u8217 ?s supreme virtue is to have solved the dilemma of adequate language. . . . he has developed a mode which is at once neutral and modern, lyric yet full of technical resource. It has many of the qualities of very good prose, being at all times in forward motion and responsive to the claims of precision. But it has the economy and soar of the poet. Written in flexible blank verse, Fitzgerald\uc1 \u8217 ?s narrative moves with such ease of tread that we often forget the sheer virtuosity of the artisan. . . .  Fitzgerald\uc1 \u8217 ?s book is a primer in the vexed craft of translation.\uc1 \u8221 ? (George Steiner, }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Kenyon Review }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 1961).}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Readers who would like the full text of Fitzgerald\uc1 \u8217 ?s translation should use the following link: }{\field \fldedit {\*\fldinst {\b1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 }{\b1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  HYPERLINK "https://ia802906.us.archive.org/10/items/hmrio/The%20Odyssey%20by%20Homer%20-%20translated%20by%20Robert%20Fitzgerald.pdf" }}{\fldrslt {\b1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 }{\cs15 \b1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \cf14 \ul Fitzgerald }{\cs15 \b1 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \cf14 \ul Odyssey}}}{\cs15 \b1 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \cf14 \ul }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 .}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf8 \page }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\*\bkmkstart odysseylattimore}{\*\bkmkend odysseylattimore}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 The Odyssey of Homer}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Translated by}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Richmond Lattimore}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Chicago 1965}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Sample from the Opening of the Poem}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Tell me, Muse, of the man of many ways, who was driven}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 far journeys, after he had sacked Troy's sacred citadel.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Many were they whose cities he saw, whose minds he learned of,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 many the pains he suffered in his spirit on the wide sea,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 struggling for his own life and the homecoming of his companions.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Even so he could not save his companions, hard though}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 he strove to; they were destroyed by their own wild recklessness,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 fools, who devoured the oxen of Helios, the Sun God,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 and he took away the day of their homecoming. From some point}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 here, goddess, daughter of Zeus, speak, and begin our story.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Then all the others, as many as fled sheer destruction,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 were at home now, having escaped the sea and the fighting.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 This one alone, longing for his wife and his homecoming,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 was detained by the queenly nymph Kalypso, bright among goddesses,I}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 n her hollowed caverns, desiring that he should be her husband.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 But when in the circling of the years that very year}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 came in which the gods had spun for him his time of homecoming}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 to Ithaka, not even then was he free of his trials}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 nor among his own people. But all the gods pitied him}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 except Poseidon; he remained relentlessly angry }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 with godlike Odysseus, until his return to his own country.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 But Poseidon was gone now to visit the far Aithiopians,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Aithiopians, most distant of men, who live divided,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 some at the setting of Hyperion, some at his rising.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 to receive a hecatomb of bulls and rams. There  }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 he sat at the feast and took pleasure. Meanwhile the other}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Olympian gods were gathered together in the halls of Zeus.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 First among them to speak was the father of gods and mortals,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 for he was thinking in his heart of stately Aigisthos,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 whom Orestes, Agamemnon's far-famed son    }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 had murdered. Remembering him he spoke now before the immortals:}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \uc1 \u8216 ?Oh for shame, how the mortals put the blame upon us}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 gods, for they say evils come from us but it is they, rather,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 who by their own recklessness win sorrow beyond what is given,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 as now lately, beyond what was given, Aigisithos}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 married the wife of Atreus' son and murdered him on his homecoming,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 though he knew it was sheer destruction, for we ourselves had told him,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 sending Hermes, the mighty watcher, Argeiphontes,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 not to kill the man, nor court his lady in marriage;}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 for vengeance would come on him from Orestes, }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 son of Atreides, whenever he came of age and longed for his own country.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 So Hermes told him, but for all his kind intentions he could not}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 persuade the mind of Aigisthos. And now he was paid for everything.'}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 REVIEW COMMENT}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Richmond Lattimore's translation of the }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Odysssey}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 , like his }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Iliad}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 , has received fulsome praise, more so than any other recent translation. And the two books are firmly established as the favourites of the professoriate. Yet many readers find his translations--offerred to us as poetry (hexameters)--almost unreadable:}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 It is incredible that a man who can write English poetry, who has written fine translations . . .  could abandon English for the worst translationese. . . . [Lattimore] gets some things right now that were botched in }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 The Iliad}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  . . . but he still does not think the thing into English. . . . [The] cause for so dismal an effect [is his] conception of fidelity to the Homeric hexameter. . . . To achieve mathematical faithfulness, he sacrifices the primary esthetic effect, which is one of formality and control. . . . Lattimore distorts the order of English, and stumbles, often, into ambiguity. . . . The result of his narrow minded focus and literalism in the handling of separate units is the lifeless  jointure of part to part . . . an effect the very opposite of . . . [that] made possible by oral poetry's large formulaic and rhythmic building blocks\uc1 \u8221 ? (Gary Wills, }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 National Review}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  1968)}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 There is not enough space here to explore this curious difference of opinion. Perhaps I shall do so at a later date. Such an investigation might reveal some interesting facts about the evaluating criteria of the scholarly establishment. Meanwhile, here are some comments in praise of Lattimore:}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 It would be a crime to underestimate the miraculous and self-effacing artistry with which Professor Lattimore has reanimated Homer for this generation and perhaps for other generations to come" }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Times Literary Supplement}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  (London)}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Lattimore's translation of Homer's }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Odyssey}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  is the most eloquent, persuasive, and imaginative I have  seen. It reads as if the poem had originally been written in English. (Paul Engle)}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li720 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin720 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 The best . . . translator of Greek poetry  into English is Richmond Lattimore. . . . This is the best }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Odyssey}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  in modern English. (Gilbert Highet).}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \lo