2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 GODDESS of song, teach me the story of a hero.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \fi240 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 This was the man of wide-ranging spirit who had sacked the sacred town of Troy and who wandered afterwards long and far. Many were those who cities he viewed and whose minds he came to know, many the troubles that vexed his heart as he sailed the seas, labouring to save himself and to bring his comrades home. But his comrades he could not keep from ruin, strive as he might; they perished instead by their own presumptuousness. Fools, they devoured the cattle of Hyperion, and he, the sun-god, cut off from them the day of their homecoming.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \fi240 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8      Goddess, daughter of Zeus, to me in turn impart some knowledge of all these things, beginning where you will.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \fi240 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8      The tale begins when all those others who had escaped the pit of destruction were safe in their own lands, spared by the wars and seax.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Only Odysseus was held elsewhere, pining for home and wife; the nymph Calypso, a goddess of strange power and beauty, had kept him captive within her arching caverns, yearning for him to be her husband. And when there came with revolving seasons the year that the gods had set for his journey home to Ithaca, not even then was he past his troubles, not even then was he with his own people. For though all the gods beside had compassion on him, Poseidon's anger was unabated against the hero until he returned to his own land.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 But now Poseidon had gone to visit the Ethiopians, those distant Ethiopians whose nation is parted within itself, so that some are near the settting and some near the rising sun, but all alike are at the world's end; to these he had gone to receive a great offering of bulls and rams, and there he was taking his pleasure now, seated at the banquet. But the other gods were gathered together in the palace of Olympian Zeus, and the father of gods and men began to speak to them. His mind was full of Lord Aegisthus, slain by renowned Orestes, the child of Agamemnon; with him in mind Zeus began to speak to the Deathless Ones.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \uc1 \u8216 ?O the waywardness of these mortals! They accuse the gods, they say that their troubles come from us, and yet by their own presumptuousness they draw down sorrow upon themselves that outruns their allotted portion. So now, Aegisthus outran his allotted portion by taking in marriage the wedded wife of the son of Atreus and killing her husband when he returned. Yet he knew what pit of destruction was before him, because we ourselves warned him of it. We sent him Hermes, the Keen Watcher, the Radiant One; we forbade him to kill the king or to woo his wife, under pain of vengeance for Agamemnon that would come upon him from Orestes when the boy grew up and felt a longing for his own country. Thus Hermes warned him, wishing him well, but Aegisthus' heart would not hear reason, and how he has paid all his debts at once.'}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 REVIEW COMMENT}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Shewring offers an accurate and direct English }{\i1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Odyssey}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  in (generally) idiomatic English. And he offers interesting footnotes throughout. Those looking for a prose translation should certainly consider using this text. }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Readers who would like a longer preview of Shewring\uc1 \u8217 ?s text should use the following link: }{\field \fldedit {\*\fldinst {\b1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 }{\b1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8  HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Odyssey-Oxford-Worlds-Classics/dp/0199536783?asin=0199536783&revisionId=&format=4&depth=1" }}{\fldrslt {\b1 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 }{\cs15 \b1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \cf14 \ul Shewring }{\cs15 \b1 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \cf14 \ul Odyssey}}}{\cs15 \b1 \i1 \fs24 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \af4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \cf14 \ul }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 .}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af5 \loch \af5 \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 {\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf8 \page }{\rtlch \fcs1 \af0 \afs24 \ltrch \fcs0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1025 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1025 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\*\bkmkstart odysseymandelbaum}{\*\bkmkend odysseymandelbaum}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 The Odyssey of Homer}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Allen Mandelbaum}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Berkeley 1990}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \qc \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 [A Sample from the Opening of the Poem]}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Muse, tell me of the man of many wiles,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the man who wandered many paths of exile}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 after he sacked Troy\uc1 \u8217 ?s sacred citadel.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 He saw the cities\uc1 \u8212 ?mapped the minds\uc1 \u8212 ?of many;}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 and on the sea, his spirit suffered every}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 adversity\uc1 \u8212 ?to keep his life intact,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 to bring his comrades back.  In that last task,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 he will was firm and fast, and yet he failed:}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 he could not save his comrades.  Fools, they foiled}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 themselves: they ate the oxen of the Sun,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the herd of H\uc1 \u233 ?lios Hyp\uc1 \u233 ?rion;}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the lord of light requited their transgression\uc1 \u8212 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 he took away the day of their return.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Muse, tell us of these matters. Daughter of Zeus,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 my starting point is any point you choose.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \par }\pard \plain \s22 \li0 \ri0 \sb100 \sa100 \sbauto1 \saauto1 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \lang1033 \langnp1033 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 {\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 All other Greeks who had been spared the steep}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 descent to death had reached their homes\uc1 \u8212 ?released}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 from war and waves.  One man alone was left,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 still longing for his home, his wife, his rest.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 For the commanding nymph, the brightest goddess,}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Calypso, held him in her hollow grottoes:}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 she wanted him as husband.  Even when}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the wheel of years drew near his destined time\uc1 \u8212 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 the time the gods designed for his return}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 to Ithaca\uc1 \u8212 ?he still could not depend }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 upon fair fortune or unfailing friends.}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 While other gods took pity on him, one\uc1 \u8212 ?}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 Poseidon\uc1 \u8212 ?still pursued: he preyed upon}{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 \line }{\fs24 \rtlch \alang1 \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af4 \loch \f4 \lang4105 \langnp4105 \langfe2052 \langfenp2052 \alang1 \cf8 divine Odysseus until the